<pre class=metadata>
Title: The Collector Element
Shortname: collector-element
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/HTML-Additions/collector-element/spec/
Repository: arronei/HTML-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification extends HTML with a <code>collector</code> element. A collector groups
    the <{input}> and <{select}> elements that hold the pieces of one value, such as the parts of a
    telephone number or a date. Its <code>pattern</code> attribute is a template that says how the
    pieces combine, for example <code>({areaCode}) {centralOfficeCode}-{lineNumber}</code>. The
    collector submits the combined value under its own name, and it is validated as a whole: it is
    invalid while the pattern is only partly filled in, or while any of its pieces is invalid, and it
    reports one error message for the whole value.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css no
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

